          "path": "_m/u/1/2/2/clare-castle-wp/clare-station-the-goods-shed-g.jpg",
          "filename": "Clare station - the goods shed (geograph 2072124).jpg",
          "caption": "Clare station - the goods shed. Clare motte and castle can be seen in the background. Clare station is situated in the grounds of Clare Castle. It was opened in 1865 by the Great Eastern Railway as an extension of the already existing line between Marks Tey and Sudbury. It closed in 1967. The station has been preserved and presently forms part of Clare Country Park. All the station buildings including the goods shed are still in place. The latter retains a short section of track and a crane and is now the visitor centre for the country park.",
          "alt": "Clare station - the goods shed. Clare motte and castle can be seen in the background. Clare station is situated in the grounds of Clare Castle. It was opened in 1865 by the Great Eastern Railway as an extension of the already existing line between Marks Tey and Sudbury. It closed in 1967. The station has been preserved and presently forms part of Clare Country Park. All the station buildings including the goods shed are still in place. The latter retains a short section of track and a crane and is now the visitor centre for the country park.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 467,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
          "artist": "Evelyn Simak",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clare_station_-_the_goods_shed_(geograph_2072124).jpg",
          "sourceType": "commons-category",
          "sourceArticleId": "clare-castle-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "u122"
        },
        {
          "path": "_m/u/1/2/2/clare-castle-wp/clare-castle-geograph-2072116-.jpg",
          "filename": "Clare Castle - geograph-2072116-by-Evelyn-Simak.jpg",
          "caption": "Beacon by Clare CastleThe 13th century stone castle keep is set upon its 70ft high motte, situated in Clare Country Park, and accessible via a winding footpath. It overlooks the town as well as its inner and outer baileys. The inner bailey contains the former Clare railway station &gt; 2072126 and the goods yard, which operated for over 100 years, with the goods shed &gt; 2072121 now housing the visitor centre and railway displays.",
          "alt": "Beacon by Clare CastleThe 13th century stone castle keep is set upon its 70ft high motte, situated in Clare Country Park, and accessible via a winding footpath. It overlooks the town as well as its inner and outer baileys. The inner bailey contains the former Clare railway station &gt; 2072126 and the goods yard, which operated for over 100 years, with the goods shed &gt; 2072121 now housing the visitor centre and railway displays.",
          "width": 640,
          "height": 512,
